# Alpine minirootfs provides /bin/sh, BusyBox applets, udhcpc, nc, and base device/mount tooling.
# Docker static provides dockerd, containerd, runc, docker-init, docker-proxy, ctr, and docker.
# crun is a faster optional OCI runtime; Dory keeps its runc-compatible path as the default.
# Apple Silicon GPU mode additionally embeds Dory's production Venus runtime pack plus a pinned
# Debian Bookworm glibc Vulkan-Tools closure from the same snapshot timestamp as guest/mesa/PINS. The
# engine rootfs stays Alpine/musl for PID 1 and Docker, while /usr/bin/vulkaninfo runs through
# Debian's AArch64 glibc loader and is forced at boot to enumerate only Dory's tuple-bound
# /opt/dory/mesa Venus ICD. Do not replace this with distro Mesa drivers.
# Apple Silicon additionally embeds Dory's hash-locked FEX-Emu 2607 binaries, built from the
# pinned tag plus Dory's container integration and signal-context patches, and the upstream
# ProcessorID stack fix. The FEX executables are static PIE so
# they survive nested chroots and remain relocatable around guest VMA reservations. The patch also
# preserves Linux shebang, descriptor-exec, argument-vector, and guest-seccomp semantics through
# nested process chains. Its compiler inputs are independently pinned by the vendor Dockerfile's
# Ubuntu snapshot and BUILD_PACKAGES.txt inventory; the packages below supply upstream data files
# and licensing notices.
